module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineDifferentialsIso.Surjective
public import StacksFrontier.Topology.Sheaves.Basis.ModuleRestriction

/-!
# The sheaf of relative differentials from its values on affine opens

Let `f : X ⟶ S` be a morphism of schemes. The affine opens `U ⊆ X` which map into some affine
open `V ⊆ S` form a basis of the topology of `X`. On such a `U`, with `A = Γ(X, U)` and
`R = Γ(S, V)`, put `Γ(U, Ω) = Ω_{A/R}`. For `U' ⊆ U` in the basis the restriction map
`Ω_{A/R} ⟶ Ω_{A'/R'}` is the additive map sending `d a` to `d (a|_{U'})`, and these data form a
sheaf of modules on the basis over the restriction of `𝒪_X`. Its restriction maps are uniquely
determined by that formula, since `Ω_{A/R}` is generated by the `d a` as an `A`-module. This
sheaf on the basis is the restriction of the sheaf of relative differentials `Ω_{X/S}`, and
since restriction to a basis is an equivalence on sheaves of modules, it determines `Ω_{X/S}`
up to isomorphism. This is the second construction of `Ω_{X/S}` described in
[Stacks, Tag 01UU].

## Main definitions

* `PresheafOfModules.copyObj`: a presheaf of modules with its modules of sections replaced by
  isomorphic ones, and `PresheafOfModules.isoCopyObj`, the isomorphism with the original.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.affineOpensOver`: the affine opens of `X` mapping into an
  affine open of `S`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver`: the presheaf of modules on that
  basis with sections `Ω_{A/R}`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.kaehlerSheafOnAffineOpensOver`: the same, as a sheaf of
  modules on the basis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.restrictRelativeDifferentialsIso`: the restriction of
  `Ω_{X/S}` to the basis is this sheaf.

## Main results

* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isBasis_affineOpensOver`: these opens form a basis.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver_map_d`: the restriction maps send
  `d a` to `d (a|_{U'})`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.isSheaf_kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver`: the sheaf condition.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.restrictRelativeDifferentialsIso_hom_app_d`: the comparison
  with `Ω_{X/S}` sends `d_{X/S} a` to `d a`.
* `AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom.nonempty_iso_relativeDifferentials_iff`: a sheaf of
  `𝒪_X`-modules is isomorphic to `Ω_{X/S}` if and only if its restriction to the basis is
  isomorphic to the sheaf with sections `Ω_{A/R}`.

## Implementation notes

The value `Ω_{A/R}` depends on a choice of affine open `V ⊆ S` with `U ⊆ f⁻¹ V`; one such `V`
is fixed for each `U` (`affineOpensOverBase`). Any other choice gives a canonically isomorphic
module, both being identified with `Γ(U, Ω_{X/S})`.

The algebraic preliminaries the remark alludes to, needed to construct the restriction maps and
verify the sheaf condition directly, are replaced by the identification of Stacks 01UT,
`Γ(U, Ω_{X/S}) ≅ Ω_{A/R}` compatibly with the universal derivations: the restriction maps are
transported along it, and the sheaf condition is inherited from `Ω_{X/S}`. The formula
`kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver_map_d` shows that the transported maps are the algebraic ones, and it
characterizes them, since a semilinear map out of `Ω_{A/R}` is determined by its values on the
`d a`.

The basis is viewed as a site through `BasisCat`, with the topology induced from `X`, and the
equivalence between sheaves of modules on `X` and on the basis is
`isEquivalence_restrictModuleSheaf` (Stacks 009U).

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 01UU](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01UU)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 01UT](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/01UT)
* [Stacks Project, Tag 009U](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/009U)
-/

@[expose] public section

open CategoryTheory AlgebraicGeometry TopologicalSpace Opposite

universe v u

namespace PresheafOfModules

variable {C : Type*} [Category C] {R : Cᵒᵖ ⥤ RingCat.{u}}

/-- A presheaf of modules with its modules of sections replaced by isomorphic ones. -/
noncomputable def copyObj (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (obj : ∀ X, ModuleCat.{v} (R.obj X))
    (e : ∀ X, M.obj X ≅ obj X) : PresheafOfModules.{v} R where
  obj := obj
  map {X Y} f := (e X).inv ≫ M.map f ≫ (ModuleCat.restrictScalars (R.map f).hom).map (e Y).hom
  map_id X := by
    ext x
    simp only [PresheafOfModules.map_id]
    exact (e X).inv_hom_id_apply x
  map_comp f g := by
    ext x
    simp
    rfl

/-- The modules of sections of `M.copyObj obj e` are the given modules `obj X`. -/
@[simp]
lemma copyObj_obj (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (obj : ∀ X, ModuleCat.{v} (R.obj X))
    (e : ∀ X, M.obj X ≅ obj X) (X : Cᵒᵖ) : (M.copyObj obj e).obj X = obj X := rfl

/-- The restriction maps of `M.copyObj obj e` are those of `M` conjugated by the
isomorphisms `e`. -/
lemma copyObj_map_apply (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (obj : ∀ X, ModuleCat.{v} (R.obj X))
    (e : ∀ X, M.obj X ≅ obj X) {X Y : Cᵒᵖ} (f : X ⟶ Y) (x : obj X) :
    (M.copyObj obj e).map f x = (e Y).hom (M.map f ((e X).inv x)) := rfl

/-- A presheaf of modules is isomorphic to its copy along isomorphisms of sections. -/
noncomputable def isoCopyObj (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (obj : ∀ X, ModuleCat.{v} (R.obj X))
    (e : ∀ X, M.obj X ≅ obj X) : M ≅ M.copyObj obj e :=
  isoMk e fun X Y f => by
    ext x
    exact congrArg (fun y => (e Y).hom (M.map f y)) ((e X).hom_inv_id_apply x).symm

/-- The components of the forward map of `M.isoCopyObj obj e` are the isomorphisms `e X`. -/
@[simp]
lemma isoCopyObj_hom_app (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (obj : ∀ X, ModuleCat.{v} (R.obj X))
    (e : ∀ X, M.obj X ≅ obj X) (X : Cᵒᵖ) : (M.isoCopyObj obj e).hom.app X = (e X).hom := rfl

/-- The components of the inverse map of `M.isoCopyObj obj e` are the inverses of `e X`. -/
@[simp]
lemma isoCopyObj_inv_app (M : PresheafOfModules.{v} R) (obj : ∀ X, ModuleCat.{v} (R.obj X))
    (e : ∀ X, M.obj X ≅ obj X) (X : Cᵒᵖ) : (M.isoCopyObj obj e).inv.app X = (e X).inv := rfl

end PresheafOfModules

namespace AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

open Stacks.BasisRestriction

variable {X S : Scheme.{u}} (f : X ⟶ S)

/-- The affine opens of `X` mapping into an affine open of `S`. -/
def affineOpensOver : Set X.Opens :=
  {U | IsAffineOpen U ∧ ∃ V : S.Opens, IsAffineOpen V ∧ U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V}

/-- An open `U` of `X` lies in `f.affineOpensOver` if and only if it is affine and contained in
the preimage of an affine open of `S`. -/
theorem mem_affineOpensOver {U : X.Opens} :
    U ∈ f.affineOpensOver ↔ IsAffineOpen U ∧ ∃ V : S.Opens, IsAffineOpen V ∧ U ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ V :=
  Iff.rfl

/-- **The affine opens over affine opens form a basis.** The affine opens of `X` mapping into
an affine open of `S` form a basis of the topology of `X`. -/
@[stacks 01UU "the affine opens mapping into an affine open of the base form a basis"]
theorem isBasis_affineOpensOver : Opens.IsBasis f.affineOpensOver := by
  rw [Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd]
  intro W x hx
  obtain ⟨V, hV, hfx, -⟩ := (Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp S.isBasis_affineOpens)
    (show f.base x ∈ (⊤ : S.Opens) from trivial)
  obtain ⟨U, hU, hxU, hUle⟩ := (Opens.isBasis_iff_nbhd.mp X.isBasis_affineOpens)
    (show x ∈ W ⊓ f ⁻¹ᵁ V from ⟨hx, hfx⟩)
  exact ⟨U, ⟨hU, V, hV, hUle.trans inf_le_right⟩, hxU, hUle.trans inf_le_left⟩

/-- An affine open of `S` over which a member of `f.affineOpensOver` lies, chosen once and for
all. -/
noncomputable def affineOpensOverBase (U : BasisCat f.affineOpensOver) : S.Opens :=
  U.property.2.choose

/-- The chosen affine open of the base is affine. -/
theorem isAffineOpen_affineOpensOverBase (U : BasisCat f.affineOpensOver) :
    IsAffineOpen (f.affineOpensOverBase U) := U.property.2.choose_spec.1

/-- A member of the basis lies over its chosen affine open of the base. -/
theorem le_preimage_affineOpensOverBase (U : BasisCat f.affineOpensOver) :
    U.obj ≤ f ⁻¹ᵁ f.affineOpensOverBase U := U.property.2.choose_spec.2

/-- The Kähler differentials `Ω_{A/R}` of `R = Γ(S, V) ⟶ A = Γ(X, U)` for a member `U` of
`f.affineOpensOver` lying over the affine open `V = f.affineOpensOverBase U`. -/
noncomputable abbrev affineOpensOverKaehler
    (U : BasisCat f.affineOpensOver) : ModuleCat.{u} Γ(X, U.obj) :=
  CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential
    (f.appLE (f.affineOpensOverBase U) U.obj (f.le_preimage_affineOpensOverBase U))

/-- The comparison map of Stacks 01UT is an isomorphism on the members of the basis. -/
instance (U : BasisCat f.affineOpensOver) :
    IsIso (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineDifferentials.kaehlerToSections f
      (f.affineOpensOverBase U) U.obj (f.le_preimage_affineOpensOverBase U)) :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineDifferentialsIso.isIso_kaehlerToSections f U.property.1
    (f.le_preimage_affineOpensOverBase U) (f.isAffineOpen_affineOpensOverBase U)

/-- The identification of Stacks 01UT of the sections of `Ω_{X/S}` over a member of the basis
with the Kähler differentials `Ω_{A/R}`. -/
noncomputable def relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler
    (U : BasisCat f.affineOpensOver) :
    (relativeDifferentials f).val.obj (op U.obj) ≅ f.affineOpensOverKaehler U :=
  (asIso (Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineDifferentials.kaehlerToSections f
    (f.affineOpensOverBase U) U.obj (f.le_preimage_affineOpensOverBase U))).symm

/-- The identification of Stacks 01UT sends `d_{X/S} a` to `d a`. -/
theorem relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler_hom_d
    (U : BasisCat f.affineOpensOver) (a : Γ(X, U.obj)) :
    (f.relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler U).hom.hom
        ((universalRelativeDerivation f).d a) = CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential.d a := by
  rw [← Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineDifferentials.kaehlerToSections_d f
    (f.affineOpensOverBase U) U.obj (f.le_preimage_affineOpensOverBase U) a]
  exact (f.relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler U).inv_hom_id_apply _

/-- The inverse of the identification of Stacks 01UT sends `d a` to `d_{X/S} a`. -/
theorem relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler_inv_d
    (U : BasisCat f.affineOpensOver) (a : Γ(X, U.obj)) :
    (f.relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler U).inv.hom
        (CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential.d a) = (universalRelativeDerivation f).d a :=
  Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.AffineDifferentials.kaehlerToSections_d f
    (f.affineOpensOverBase U) U.obj (f.le_preimage_affineOpensOverBase U) a

/-- **The ansatz `Γ(U, Ω_{X/S}) = Ω_{A/R}`.** The presheaf of modules on the basis
`f.affineOpensOver`, over the restriction of `𝒪_X`, with sections the Kähler differentials
`Ω_{A/R}` over `U = Spec A` lying over `V = Spec R`. Its restriction maps are described by
`kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver_map_d`. -/
@[stacks 01UU "the presheaf on the basis with sections the Kähler differentials"]
noncomputable def kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver :
    _root_.PresheafOfModules.{u} (restrictRingSheafToBasis
      f.isBasis_affineOpensOver X.ringCatSheaf).val :=
  ((restrictModuleSheaf.{u, u} f.isBasis_affineOpensOver
    X.ringCatSheaf).obj (relativeDifferentials f)).val.copyObj
    (fun U => f.affineOpensOverKaehler U.unop)
    (fun U => f.relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler U.unop)

/-- **The restriction maps.** For `U' ⊆ U` in the basis, the restriction map
`Ω_{A/R} ⟶ Ω_{A'/R'}` sends `d a` to `d (a|_{U'})`. -/
@[stacks 01UU "the restriction maps"]
theorem kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver_map_d
    {U U' : BasisCat f.affineOpensOver} (i : U' ⟶ U)
    (a : Γ(X, U.obj)) :
    (f.kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver.map i.op).hom (CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential.d a) =
      CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential.d
        (X.presheaf.map ((basisInclusion _).map i).op a) :=
  (congrArg (fun y => (f.relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler U').hom.hom
    ((relativeDifferentials f).val.map ((basisInclusion _).map i).op y))
      (f.relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler_inv_d U a)).trans
    ((congrArg (f.relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler U').hom.hom
      ((universalRelativeDerivation f).d_map ((basisInclusion _).map i).op a).symm).trans
      (f.relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler_hom_d U' _))

/-- **The sheaf condition.** The presheaf with sections `Ω_{A/R}` is a sheaf on the basis. -/
@[stacks 01UU "the sheaf condition"]
theorem isSheaf_kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver :
    Presheaf.IsSheaf (basisGrothendieckTopology f.isBasis_affineOpensOver)
      f.kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver.presheaf :=
  (Presheaf.isSheaf_of_iso_iff ((_root_.PresheafOfModules.toPresheaf _).mapIso
    (_root_.PresheafOfModules.isoCopyObj _ _ _))).mp
    ((restrictModuleSheaf.{u, u} f.isBasis_affineOpensOver
      X.ringCatSheaf).obj (relativeDifferentials f)).isSheaf

/-- The sheaf of modules on the basis `f.affineOpensOver` with sections `Ω_{A/R}`. -/
noncomputable def kaehlerSheafOnAffineOpensOver :
    ModuleSheafOnBasis.{u, u} f.isBasis_affineOpensOver X.ringCatSheaf :=
  ⟨f.kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver, f.isSheaf_kaehlerOnAffineOpensOver⟩

/-- **The construction gives `Ω_{X/S}`.** The restriction of the sheaf of relative
differentials to the basis `f.affineOpensOver` is the sheaf with sections `Ω_{A/R}`; on
sections it is the identification of Stacks 01UT
(`restrictRelativeDifferentialsIso_hom_app_d`). -/
@[stacks 01UU "the sheaf on the basis is the restriction of the sheaf of differentials"]
noncomputable def restrictRelativeDifferentialsIso :
    (restrictModuleSheaf.{u, u} f.isBasis_affineOpensOver
      X.ringCatSheaf).obj (relativeDifferentials f) ≅ f.kaehlerSheafOnAffineOpensOver :=
  (SheafOfModules.fullyFaithfulForget _).preimageIso
    (_root_.PresheafOfModules.isoCopyObj _ _ _)

/-- The comparison of `Ω_{X/S}` with the sheaf on the basis sends `d_{X/S} a` to `d a`. -/
theorem restrictRelativeDifferentialsIso_hom_app_d
    (U : BasisCat f.affineOpensOver) (a : Γ(X, U.obj)) :
    (f.restrictRelativeDifferentialsIso.hom.val.app (op U)).hom
        ((universalRelativeDerivation f).d a) = CommRingCat.KaehlerDifferential.d a :=
  f.relativeDifferentialsIsoAffineOpensOverKaehler_hom_d U a

/-- **The sheaf on the basis determines `Ω_{X/S}`.** A sheaf of `𝒪_X`-modules is isomorphic to
the sheaf of relative differentials if and only if its restriction to the basis
`f.affineOpensOver` is isomorphic to the sheaf with sections `Ω_{A/R}`. -/
@[stacks 01UU "the sheaf on the basis determines the sheaf of differentials"]
theorem nonempty_iso_relativeDifferentials_iff (M : X.Modules) :
    Nonempty (M ≅ relativeDifferentials f) ↔
      Nonempty ((restrictModuleSheaf.{u, u} f.isBasis_affineOpensOver
        X.ringCatSheaf).obj M ≅ f.kaehlerSheafOnAffineOpensOver) := by
  have := isEquivalence_restrictModuleSheaf.{u, u} f.isBasis_affineOpensOver X.ringCatSheaf
  exact ⟨fun ⟨e⟩ => ⟨(restrictModuleSheaf.{u, u} f.isBasis_affineOpensOver
      X.ringCatSheaf).mapIso e ≪≫ f.restrictRelativeDifferentialsIso⟩,
    fun ⟨e⟩ => ⟨(Functor.asEquivalence (restrictModuleSheaf.{u, u}
      f.isBasis_affineOpensOver X.ringCatSheaf)).fullyFaithfulFunctor.preimageIso
      (e ≪≫ f.restrictRelativeDifferentialsIso.symm)⟩⟩

end AlgebraicGeometry.Scheme.Hom

end
